+| Q1: search (D\le400) for a screened cofinal family | **RAISE as falsification/target selection** | One closed-form survivor family would permanently stop the census-as-proof framing and give coefficient systems with repeated shape.  Failure through 400 is only data. |
+| Q1: uniform (j=2) forced-zero theorem | **RAISE, retyped statewise** | There is an exact divisor parameterization when the DP `danger` bit is still set; Idea Card 1 states it.  It is not a row-level scalar predicate once a nonzero ancestor has cleared `danger`. |
+| Q1: recover Moh's exact 1983 six-row program | **LOWER** | The historical artifact can settle provenance, not JC2.  The mathematical residual after the sourced tree is simultaneous coefficients; no desk test can recover the CDC listing (`AUDIT.md:15992-15997`). |
+| Q1: edgewise full-tree recentering | **UNCHANGED / secondary** | Potentially useful, but it changes Prop. 5.4's quantifier and still leaves excess rows.  Do not consume it before a proof. |
+| Q2: independent existence of every node's (p_v,q_v) | **RAISE, but insufficient** | The A.3 equation has an exact discriminant-saturated weighted-configuration form.  Nodewise nonemptiness must be separated from adjacent-node compatibility. |
+| Q2: simultaneous sibling coefficients | **RAISE to the principal bottleneck** | Encode it as a fibre product of the node schemes over actual edge coordinate/jet maps, then add global polynomiality.  This is the missing universal coefficient object. |
