+   method proof, not JC2.  The desired theorem says that for every full tree
+   of height at most five, some finite associated-graded Jacobian/edge/global
+   class fails.  It may depend on the whole tree; demanding a scalar formula
+   is an unnecessary restriction.
+5. **The (u_s>1) branch.**  Prop. 6.3 does not cover it.  At (D=108), one
+   of the eight stored passport-screened rows has (u_s=2); seven have
+   (u_s=1).  The p.209 minor alternatives must be compiled without calling
+   a regular dirty step an MP0 merge or silently assuming a second descent.
+6. **Screened cofinality.**  This matters for target selection and a possible
+   pure arithmetic proof, but it ranks below coefficients.  A (D\le400)
+   negative search cannot certify eventual emptiness.
+
+The lost CDC listing, edgewise recentering, and a stronger semigroup scalar
+rank below these.  They can simplify a target list; none presently attacks
+the existence of one pair.
+
+### Disproof bottlenecks, in order
+
+1. **One exact full-tree coefficient point.**  The best target is the paired
+   (D=108) data above because the two variants share scalar data but have
+   different transition histories.  A nodewise star, a formal branch prefix,
+   or a monomial-Jacobian descendant is not such a point.
+2. **Lift through descent.**  Prop. 6.3 is necessary and one-way.  Even a
+   solution of the ((18,12;\gamma^3)) descendant must be lifted through the
+   approximate-root transform and then through every sibling edge to an
+   original constant-J pair.  `SURVIVES` below that level is only a lower
+   obstruction failure.
+3. **Finish over characteristic zero with full support.**  A smooth modular
+   point is excellent search evidence and may Hensel-lift (p)-adically; it
+   is not a rational/complex polynomial point.  Rational reconstruction plus
+   exact substitution into the declared ring is required.
+4. **A repeating screened tree shape.**  A closed-form `C_FULL_TREE_ODE`
+   family would give a cofinal disproof laboratory.  It would not itself
+   realize coefficients.
+
+### Strongest proof attack
+
+Attack the (D=108\to(18,12;\gamma^3)) pair by **ramification
+absorption**, then lift the resulting obstruction into the tree coefficient
+complex.  Monomial-Jacobian pairs without inherited data are plentiful: for
+integers (d\ge r\ge1) and (a\ne0),
+
+\[
+ Q_0=\pi^d+a\gamma^r,\qquad
+ P_0=\pi^{d+1}+{d+1\over d}a\gamma^r\pi
+\]
+
+satisfy, by direct differentiation,
+
+\[
+ J(P_0,Q_0)=-{r(d+1)\over d}a^2\gamma^{2r-1}.
+\]
+
+For (d=r=2), this is
+
+\[
+ Q_0=\pi^2+a\gamma^2,\qquad
+ P_0=\pi^3+\tfrac32a\gamma^2\pi,\qquad
+ J=-3a^2\gamma^3,
+\]
+
+which has exactly the primitive (3:2,k=3) signature of the selected
+((18,12)) descendant.  Inflating (pi) to a monic approximate root (h)
+of (pi)-degree six gives
+
+\[
+ J(P_0(\gamma,h),Q_0(\gamma,h))=-3a^2\gamma^3 h_\pi.
+\]
+
+The unwanted ramification factor (h_\pi) is unavoidable under pure
+composition.  All possible existence is therefore concentrated in the
+allowed lower approximate-root corrections.  Compute the top two (h)-adic
+Jacobian blocks and prove that the inherited tree/radius supports cannot
+cancel the nonconstant part of (h_\pi).  This is a precise initial-form
+lemma with a proof-shaped generalization; it does not confuse the empty pure
+composition slice with the full pair.
+
+### Strongest counterexample attack
+
+Run the same fork in the opposite direction: solve for the **smallest exact
+correction support that does absorb (h_\pi)** for either of the two
+((18,12;\gamma^3)) inherited trees.  If a component survives, require a
+smooth point after discriminant/leader/(c) saturation, extend one tree page,
+then solve the inverse Prop. 6.3 edge equations.  Only after the complete
+((108,72)) polynomial pair passes (J\in k^*), all degree leaders, and the
+full tree/global polynomiality conditions is it counterexample evidence.
+The degree pair (108,72) cannot be the degree pair of a plane polynomial
+automorphism, so an exact original Keller point would be decisive; the
+descendant alone would not be.
+
+## 4. Idea cards (three maximum)
+
+### Card 1 — the exact sibling scheme: barycentric nodes, edge fibre product
+
+**Mechanism.**  At a full-tree node (v), write (P=P_v=\deg p_v),
+(Q=Q_v=\deg q_v), let (a_1,\ldots,a_Q) be the distinct roots of the
+squarefree (q_v), and let (u_i=\operatorname{mult}_{a_i}p_v), including
+(u_i=0) at unused (q)-roots.  Define (w_i=P-Qu_i).  Prop. A.3 is
+
+\[
+Pp_vq_v'-Qq_vp_v'=c_vp_v,\qquad c_v\ne0.
+\]
+
+At (a_i), the reviewed local calculation gives
+
+\[
+w_iq_v'(a_i)=c_v.                                      \tag{4.1}
+\]
+
+The standard barycentric identities
+(sum_i a_i^j/q_v'(a_i)=0) for (0\le j\le Q-2) therefore turn A.3 into
+the weighted Vandermonde equations
+
+\[
+\sum_{i=1}^{Q}w_i a_i^j=0\quad(0\le j\le Q-2),\qquad
+\sum_iw_i a_i^{Q-1}=c_v                              \tag{4.2}
+\]
+
+when (q_v) is monic.  Conversely, after saturating by
+(Delta(q_v)c_v) and imposing (w_i\ne0), (4.2) makes the vector
+((w_i)) proportional to ((1/q_v'(a_i))).  The polynomial
+
+\[
+E=Pq_v'-Qq_vp_v'/p_v
+\]
+
+then has degree at most (Q-1) and takes the same value (c_v) at all
+(Q) roots of (q_v), so (E=c_v) and A.3 follows.  Thus this is an exact
+node scheme, not an equation count or a passport analogy.  The local source
+identity is checked in `xmodel/whole-tree-review-grok46-20260903.md:456-492`.
+
+The uniform answer to `OPEN[SIBLING-COEFFICIENTS]` is **not** the product of
+these node schemes.  It is their fibre product over the edge transition
+maps, with the global polynomiality equations appended.  The dictionary is:
+
+| Whole-tree object | Coefficient datum |
+|---|---|
+| node (v) | one actual local factor polynomial pair (p_v,q_v), its root-position scheme (4.2), degrees (P_v,Q_v), radius and centre |
+| factor/child edge (v\to w) | a declared zero/nonzero factor label, multiplicity, coordinate substitution (\pi_v=C_{vw}(t)+t^{\delta_w-\delta_v}\pi_w), and the induced initial/jet map |
+| sibling packet | all factors in the orbit partition, including unused (q)-roots; not merely the selected (V)-flag |
+| leaf | a truncated root series (\tau_i), not automatically a physical place until the whole edge system is realized |
+| Galois orbit | the actual permutation action, stabilizer character, shared coefficients, and one integration constant per complete branch orbit |
+| ancestor | the shared outer units in (D_i=\prod_{j\ne i}(\tau_i-\tau_j)); descendants do not receive independent copies |
+| root of the tree | the invariant sums giving `DEG`, `POLY`, and `NO-RESIDUE`; distinct orbit contributions may cancel only here |
+
+This dictionary is forced by the exact tree factorizations and local/global
+separation in `xmodel/global-interpolation-sol56-20260902.md:240-392` and
+its minimal decorated input at lines 500-514.  It explicitly separates a
+cv flag, a factor root, a branch series, and any eventual physical place.
+
+**Dependencies.**  The Opus whole-tree review must pass; the screen must
+export every orbit partition, not one representative witness; edge chart
+maps and coefficient sharing must be supplied by the sibling lane; rings,
+generator order, discriminants, and every saturation factor must be explicit.
+
+**Bounded quantity and cheapest discriminator.**  Start with exactly the two
+stored (D=108) variants at
+`box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/tree-independent-passport-D48-120.json:1214`
+and `:1263`.  Solve each node scheme separately, then form only the first
+nontrivial edge fibre.  There are at most 108 root slots before orbit
+quotient and only the finitely many nodes in the emitted witness.  Emit the
+weighted equations over (mathbf Q), reduce by cyclic orbits, fix two affine
+root coordinates, and use a discriminant Rabinowitsch variable.  Hard cap:
+nine minutes and 4 GB.
+
+**Outcomes.**
+
+- Node scheme empty: a new exact local screen; replay on Moh's six before
+  any promotion.
+- All nodes nonempty but the first edge fibre empty: the first genuine
+  sibling-coefficient obstruction and the right pattern for an all-tree
+  theorem.
+- Edge fibre nonempty and smooth: a high-value counterexample seed; attach
+  one global remainder page, without calling it an actual pair.
+- Only positive-dimensional node schemes: not failure.  Compute the edge
+  elimination ideal rather than subtracting dimensions.
+
+**Stop condition.**  Stop immediately if the exporter cannot state the
+edge substitutions or supplies only a representative path.  Also stop after
+nodewise nonemptiness if edge compatibility has not been typed; do not spend
+on a product of unrelated local solutions.
+
+**Expected information gain.**  Very high.  It decides whether the first
+missing constraint is already local root position, is genuinely cross-node,
+or lies only in global polynomiality, and it gives a reusable exact object
+for every later tree.
+
+### Card 2 — Kummer/Fourier blocks and ramification absorption for (T<=4)
+
+**Mechanism and new cross-connection.**  For a monomial-Jacobian descendant
+(J(P,Q)=c\gamma^k), put (r=k+1) and (X=\gamma^r/r).  Then
+
+\[
+dP\wedge dQ=c\,dX\wedge d\pi.
+\]
+
+This is a constant-Jacobian equation over the cyclic Kummer extension
+
+\[
+k[X,\pi]\subset k[\gamma,\pi],\qquad \gamma^r=rX,
+\]
+
+not an ordinary Keller pair over (k[X,\pi]).  Decompose the free module by
+(mu_r)-character,
+
+\[
+P=\sum_{a=0}^{r-1}\gamma^aP_a(X,\pi),\qquad
+Q=\sum_{b=0}^{r-1}\gamma^bQ_b(X,\pi).
+\]
+
+After multiplying by (rX) and reducing (gamma^{a+b}) with
+(gamma^r=rX), every Jacobian coefficient belongs to a declared character
+and Newton-weight block.  The invariant block supplies (c); all other
+character blocks vanish.  The factor (r=k+1) in the p.207 radius rule is
+exactly the valuation pullback under this Kummer map.  That connects descent
+radii, row 1's monomial bracket, Galois characters, and Appendix-II support
+in one algebraic mechanism; it is not another numerical coincidence.
+
+Use the primitive pair in section 3 as a positive control.  For the live
+((18,12;\gamma^3)) target, (r=4) and a degree-six approximate root
+introduces the explicit (h_\pi) factor.  The character blocks identify the
+minimal correction modes capable of cancelling it.
+
+**Dependencies.**  First close `OPEN[DESCENT-STATE-S3]` for the two (D=108)
+variants.  Preserve their full (V'_3) data.  Compile allowed monomials from
+proved radii only.  Use the corrected Appendix-II saturation discipline.
+
+**Bounded quantity and cheapest discriminator.**  The first run has two
+targets and only the top two (h)-adic/Newton pages.  As a calibration, the
+already typed G2 system has exactly 14 (h)-coefficients, 27
+(eta)-coefficients, and (c): 42 unknowns
+(`xmodel/descent-radii-grok46-20260903.md:383-401`).  Do not launch its full
+Gröbner basis.  Emit equations once, bucket them by (r) characters and
+weight, row-reduce sparse linear pages over three good primes, and certify
+only a decisive minor over (mathbf Q).  If the (D=108) two-page system
+survives, saturate only the reduced correction ideal at (c), degree
+leaders, and discriminants.
+
+**Outcomes.**
+
+- Every allowed correction mode is forced out: a type-specific theorem (T)
+  and a plausible induction on Newton weight.
+- A smallest nonzero mode survives: the best exact correction slice for the
+  counterexample attack; solve that slice, not an arbitrary support.
+- Character blocks immediately recouple densely: the grading is still a
+  correct implementation check but not an accelerator.
+- A full descendant solution: it refutes the type-specific (T) lemma only;
+  it does not lift itself or produce a JC2 counterexample.
+
+**Stop condition.**  Stop after two pages if no variable or equation reduction
+is achieved, or at the desk resource cap.  A modular survivor is never
+reported as `SURVIVES` over (mathbf Q).
+
+**Expected information gain.**  Highest on the live frontier.  It tests a
+specific obstruction and its exact opposite on the first non-dead degree,
+while calibrating the uniform monomial-Jacobian receiver.
+
+### Card 3 — turn the (j=2) forced-zero pattern into a divisor theorem
+
+**Mechanism.**  For an (s=3) row put
+
+\[
+X=n-M_2,\quad K=d_2,\quad r=d_3,\quad v=V_3.
+\]
+
+Here (M_3=n-2), (r\mid K,X),
+(P=vK/r), (Q=vX/r), and Def. 5.1(3) gives
+
+\[
+\delta_2=1-{X(2v-r)\over vX-r}
+={X(r-v)-r\over vX-r}.
+\]
+
+Let (B=vX-r) and
+(G=\gcd(B,X(r-v)-r)=\gcd(B,r(X-2))).  The reduced denominator is
+(A_2=B/G), while Euclid gives
+
+\[
+rB-vr(X-2)=r(2v-r),\qquad G\mid r(2v-r).              \tag{4.3}
+\]
+
+If (X>K), then the major threshold (h=K/X<1).  At (s=3) the
+(j=2) parent is still `danger`.  A positive canonical zero residue
+(b_0=P\bmod A_2) is at least one, hence exceeds (h), forces a major
+zero sibling, and reaches Prop. 5.6.  Survival therefore requires
+(A_2\mid P), and consequently
+
+\[
+vX-r\mid vK(2v-r).                                    \tag{4.4}
+\]
+
+For fixed ((K,r,v)), (X=(d+r)/v) comes from a divisor
+(d\mid vK(2v-r)) with (d\equiv-r\pmod v).  This is an exact finite
+parameterization, not a ceiling and not sufficiency.
+
+For (s>3), fix the entire higher DP state and set
+
+\[
+C=\prod_{j=3}^{s}(V_j(n-M_j)-d_j),\quad
+E=(n-M_s-1)\prod_{j=4}^{s}(V_j(n-M_{j-1})-d_j),
+\]
+
+with (L=L_2).  Then (L\delta_2=U(X)/W(X)), where
+
+\[
+U=L[(EV_3-C)X-Ed_3],\qquad W=E(V_3X-d_3),
+\]
+
+and the content-correct statement is
+
+\[
+\gcd(U(X),W(X))\mid |LEd_3C|.                         \tag{4.5}
+\]
+
+On a still-dangerous (j=2) state with (X>K), the same reasoning makes
+(W(X)) divide a fixed statewise carrier after primitive reduction.  A
+nonzero ancestor can clear `danger`, so (4.5) must be a DP-state rule, never
+a scalar row filter.
+
+**Dependencies.**  The promoted `danger` semantics and full higher
+(V)-tuple; exact reduced denominators; no edgewise recenter conjecture.
+
+**Bounded quantity and cheapest discriminator.**  Verify (4.4) on every
+(s=3) member among the 2,824 `C_FULL_TREE_ODE` assignments through
+(D\le200), then emit the primitive carrier divided by (N) on every
+still-dangerous (j=2) state through (D\le400).  This is integer
+arithmetic in the running screen, expected seconds and under 1 GB.
+
+**Outcomes.**
+
+- Carrier/(N) is uniformly bounded and divisor choices stabilize: promote
+  a precise all-degree lemma target coupling the pin to (4.5).
+- It grows on a screened parametric family: stop the skeleton-ceiling route
+  and bank that family as the coefficient/counterexample target list.
+- The equivalence fails on a control: repair denominator/content or danger
+  propagation; no mathematical inference.
+
+**Stop condition.**  One growing exact family, or any need to discard the
+full DP state, stops the ceiling claim.  No extrapolation from (D\le400).
+
+**Expected information gain.**  High at negligible cost.  It either exposes
+the arithmetic theorem behind the repeated (b_{\min}>h) kills or turns
+screened cofinality into a concrete family problem.
